  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>TLV-TVM (Transports Littoral Varois) runs the shortest and most frequent service to Porquerolles, departing from La Tour Fondue on the Giens peninsula — a crossing of about 15 minutes. The company also serves Port-Cros and Le Levant, but from the port of Hyères (Port Gavine landing stage).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to TLV-TVM's FAQ, animals travel free, dogs on a leash or in a carrier, and the website states that dogs are not allowed on the beaches. Once there, restrictions are set by the islands' manager (Port-Cros National Park): check before you leave. On <strong>Port-Cros</strong>, TLV-TVM says dogs are allowed on a leash only in the port; animals are prohibited on the rest of the island.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Port-Cros is very restrictive for dogs (port only); check the National Park's regulations before choosing your island.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Giens peninsula, with its salt-pan trail, is well suited to a walk before or after the crossing.</p>
